{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794778894,"nonce":"f4znfdLIWDuxumC22DTWp97Czb0=","title":"A layer-effect pass does not move a path clip that follows rows","message":"`GpuRenderer::resolve_node_slot` (used where layers.rs offsets primitives into a layer's frame for effects) applies a primitive's rows on the CPU one primitive at a time, with no aux rows at hand, so a path clip marked by `set_node_path_from` stays where it was painted in that pass. `with_node_rows_applied` (layered overlays) and the CPU rows backend do move it via `node_table::follow_path_clip`.\n\nA spinner inside an element with a layer effect that rows move would draw its arc clipped at the painted pose while the arc moves. Fix by passing the layer batch's aux data so the pass can call `follow_path_clip`, or by declining rows for a path-clipped primitive under a layer effect.","files":null}]}